{
    "word": "lovingkindness",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "321f72ea-1dba-3529-8fdc-f69d077a7956",
                "word": "lovingkindness",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a0865ddb-f017-4b9d-bde6-dbe29f7705d6",
                        "entry_id": "321f72ea-1dba-3529-8fdc-f69d077a7956",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "lovingkindnesses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b1ed4377-ca33-3918-9c38-852fcdc7e622",
                        "entry_id": "321f72ea-1dba-3529-8fdc-f69d077a7956",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Kindness or mercy which is based on, or arises from, love; (countable) an act of such kindness or mercy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7841881-2647-4818-914a-643680cfa6a0",
                                "sense_id": "b1ed4377-ca33-3918-9c38-852fcdc7e622",
                                "text": "But let him that glorieth, glory in this, that hee vnderſtandeth and knoweth me, that I am the Lord which exerciſe louing kindneſſe, iudgement, and righteouſneſſe in the earth: for in these things I delight, ſaith the Lord."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e61d3240-07a8-42c9-a5ca-1267473ada33",
                                "sense_id": "b1ed4377-ca33-3918-9c38-852fcdc7e622",
                                "text": "[…] My loving kindneſſe, my mercifull diſposition is a great bond, but my faithfulneſſe ſhall binde me also, I will be content to ingage my ſelfe to you, to ingage all that I am, and all that I have to you, that you may certainly confide in me, ſo as you may not onely expect it from my love, but challenge it from my faithfulneſſe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "95f22db3-5f83-43a7-84df-1ca6ee42283b",
                                "sense_id": "b1ed4377-ca33-3918-9c38-852fcdc7e622",
                                "text": "What a comfort is it for chriſtian friends to relate to each other the loving-kindneſs of the Lord? O let his praiſes be ever in our mouths, that we may be telling of his ſalvation from day to day."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "875876fa-f784-4a00-a408-7004fd1a038a",
                                "sense_id": "b1ed4377-ca33-3918-9c38-852fcdc7e622",
                                "text": "Awake, my soul, to joyful lays, / And sing the great Redeemer's praise; / He justly claims a song from me: / His loving-kindness, oh, how free!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "514ff320-d3d0-4c7c-9259-b86baa21d3bd",
                                "sense_id": "b1ed4377-ca33-3918-9c38-852fcdc7e622",
                                "text": "Have we ever had the shadow of a reason to doubt our Father's goodness? Have not His loving-kindnesses been marvellous? Has he once failed to justify our trust? Ah, no! our God has not left us at any time."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9997bdf4-3c68-4321-a4ee-96501c78b41e",
                                "sense_id": "b1ed4377-ca33-3918-9c38-852fcdc7e622",
                                "text": "In just the same way, the force of metta, lovingkindness, allows us to cohere, to come together within ourselves and with all beings. The beauty of this truth moved the Buddha to say that sustaining a loving heart, even for the duration of the snap of a finger, makes one a truly spiritual being."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae1ba78f-04f2-4b5b-91db-5619c14ea74f",
                                "sense_id": "b1ed4377-ca33-3918-9c38-852fcdc7e622",
                                "text": "When we look at the grains of sand – countless in number – they speak to us of the multitude of God's lovingkindnesses to us."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7caff679-1bd1-48ed-97bb-40df39e8f4f5",
                                "sense_id": "b1ed4377-ca33-3918-9c38-852fcdc7e622",
                                "text": "After you have spent your second week of meditation on developing mindfulness, your third week of meditation will involve developing lovingkindness. Lovingkindness Meditation, which is the third core practice, focuses bringing love, compassion, sympathy, and joy into your life."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
